        "y": 18
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Continuous CPU profiling is **opt-in** (`PERFLAB_CONTINUOUS_PROFILING=1` or PerfLab `--continuous-profiling`) and perturbs the process. Hold the same setting on baseline and candidate.\n\n- Grafana Profiles Drilldown: [/a/grafana-pyroscope-app](/a/grafana-pyroscope-app)\n- Pyroscope datasource UID: `pyroscope` (direct backend `http://127.0.0.1:4040`)\n- Selector: `process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds{service_name=~\"$service\",perf_run_id=~\"$run\"}`\n- Evidence capture uses the exact measurement window rather than a static `perf_phase` label.\n\n**Correlation path (one Grafana):** Prometheus exemplar \u2192 trace (Tempo) \u2192 **Logs for this span** (Loki, `trace_id`) and **Request rate** (Prometheus); a Loki line's `trace_id` links back to its trace. **Trace \u2192 profile:** Grafana shows a span-level profile button only for spans tagged `pyroscope.profile.id` (span-profiles SDK, not carried by the lab apps); use Explore **Split** \u2192 Pyroscope \u2192 `{service_name=\"<service>\"}` to see the span's service over the trace's time range.\n"
      },
      "description": "Deep-link into Grafana Profiles Drilldown for the selected service and run."
    }
  ],
